      "narrative": "Pima County home prices were broadly flat to slightly lower in October 2026: Redfin reported a median sale price of $353,810, down 1.4% year over year, while Realtor.com reported a median asking price of $375,000, down 2.6%.[1][7] Inventory increased, with 4,237 active listings, up 6.3% year over year, and another local report counted 4,645 homes on the market, equivalent to about 5.2 months of supply.[2][7] Sales volume weakened, with 888 October closings versus 1,075 a year earlier, indicating that buyers had more negotiating leverage while the market remained broadly balanced.[2] Local housing demand continues to draw support from the University of Arizona, defense, healthcare, and aerospace employers, while a county economic plan has attracted more than $3.6 billion in investment and approximately 3,000 construction jobs.[8][10]",
